/-!
# Independence of the algebraic upper shriek functor of its presentation

`Dualizing.PolynomialPresentation.upperShriekFunctor` is attached to a presentation of a
finite type homomorphism `f : R →+* A` as a quotient of a polynomial algebra, and genuinely
depends on that presentation.  This file proves that its isomorphism class does not: the
functors attached to any two polynomial presentations of the same `f` are naturally
isomorphic.  This is [Stacks, Tag 0BZJ].

## Main definitions

* `Dualizing.PolynomialEvalDuality` — [Stacks, Tag 0BZH] read at the evaluation surjections
  `B[x] ↠ B`, the one input of Tag 0BZJ not proved in this file; it is proved as
  `Dualizing.polynomialEvalDuality`.

## Main results

* `Dualizing.PolynomialPresentation.upperShriekFunctorIsoOfRingEquiv` — two presentations
  identified by a ring isomorphism of their polynomial algebras over `R` and over `A` give
  isomorphic functors.  This is unconditional.
* `Dualizing.PolynomialPresentation.upperShriekFunctor_iso` — Tag 0BZJ itself, conditional
  on `Dualizing.PolynomialEvalDuality`, which is discharged downstream in
  `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Dualizing/UpperShriek/PolynomialEvalDualityProof.lean`; the
  unconditional statement is
  `Dualizing.PolynomialPresentation.nonempty_upperShriekFunctor_iso` there.

## Implementation notes

The source argument is: given presentations `ψ₁ : R[x_1, …, x_n] ↠ A` and
`ψ₂ : R[y_1, …, y_m] ↠ A`, both are refined by `R[x_1, …, x_n, y_1, …, y_m] ↠ A`, and the
comparison with a refinement adding one variable is `χ = ψ ∘ π` for the `P`-algebra map
`π : P[y] → P` with `π(y) = g`, where `ψ(g)` is the image of `y`.  Then `χ^!` and
`ψ^! ∘ π^!` are both right adjoint to restriction of scalars, and `π^!` is derived base
change along `π` shifted by `-1`, which cancels the extra variable in the shift defining
upper shriek.

The last step is [Stacks, Tag 0BZH] at `π`, whose kernel is generated by the nonzerodivisor
`y - g`.  The instance of it that the argument needs is the explicit hypothesis
`Dualizing.PolynomialEvalDuality` of
`Dualizing.PolynomialPresentation.upperShriekFunctor_iso`.  It is proved as
`Dualizing.polynomialEvalDuality` in
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Dualizing/UpperShriek/PolynomialEvalDualityProof.lean`, which imports
this file, and the statement without the hypothesis is
`Dualizing.PolynomialPresentation.nonempty_upperShriekFunctor_iso` there.

Everything is proved first in a single ring universe and then transported along
`ULift.ringEquiv`, because the comparison of adjoints is only available when the module
universe and the ring universe agree.  Tag 0BZJ holds at an independent module universe:
`Dualizing.PolynomialEvalDuality` quantifies over every ring of its universe, so it is used at
`max v u` and the lift is done internally.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BZJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BZJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BZH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BZH)
-/

@[expose] public section

